{"availability":"available","full":"dotnet/orleans","name":"orleans","description":"Cloud Native application framework for .NET","category":"Developer tools","language":"C#","stars":10895,"forks":2136,"created":"2014-12-19T14:32:50Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:18:09Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dotnet.github.io/orleans/","topics":["actor-model","actors","cloud-computing","cloud-native","concurrency","distributed-actors","distributed-systems","dotnet","orleans"],"demo":"https://dotnet.github.io/orleans/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:48:03.891Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:48:03.891Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:48:03.891Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T22:54:52.756Z","stars":10896,"forks":2135},{"at":"2026-10-09T05:48:03.891Z","stars":10895,"forks":2136}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Orleans builds on the developer productivity of .NET and brings it to the world of distributed applications, such as cloud services. Orleans scales from a single on-premises server to globally distributed, highly-available applications in the cloud.","Orleans takes familiar concepts like objects, interfaces, async/await, and try/catch and extends them to multi-server environments. As such, it helps developers experienced with single-server applications transition to building resilient, scalable cloud services and other distributed applications. For this reason, Orleans has often been referred to as \"Distributed .NET\".","It was created by Microsoft Research and introduced the Virtual Actor Model as a novel approach to building a new generation of distributed systems for the Cloud era. The core contribution of Orleans is its programming model which tames the complexity inherent to highly-parallel distributed systems without restricting capabilities or imposing onerous constraints on the developer."],"features":["Orleans is a feature-rich framework. It provides a set of services that enable the development of distributed systems. The following sections describe the features of Orleans.","Orleans provides a simple persistence model which ensures that state is available to a grain before requests are processed and that consistency is maintained. Grains can have multiple named persistent data objects, for…","In addition to the simple persistence model described above, grains can have transactional state. Multiple grains can participate in ACID transactions together regardless of where their state is ultimately stored.…","Streams help developers to process series of data items in near-real time. Streams in Orleans are managed: streams do not need to be created or registered before a grain or client publishes to a stream or subscribes to…","Streams supports batch delivery of messages to consumers to improve efficiency and recovery performance. Streams are backed by queueing services such as Azure Event Hubs, Amazon Kinesis, and others. An arbitrary number…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dotnet/orleans/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0e94c27809cab30ae833945d7573956726a4fe55b16b1dbbfc16a715e39d0a82","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:52.880Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:52.880Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Orleans builds on the developer productivity of .NET and brings it to the world of distributed applications, such as cloud services. Orleans scales from a single on-premises server to globally distributed, highly-available applications in the cloud.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dotnet/orleans/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Orleans takes familiar concepts like objects, interfaces, async/await, and try/catch and extends them to multi-server environments. As such, it helps developers experienced with single-server applications transition to building resilient, scalable cloud services and other distributed applications. For this reason, Orleans has often been referred to as \"Distributed .NET\".","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dotnet/orleans/blob/main/README.md"},{"text":"Streams help developers to process series of data items in near-real time. Streams in Orleans are managed: streams do not need to be created or registered before a grain or client publishes to a stream or subscribes to…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dotnet/orleans/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"0e94c27809cab30ae833945d7573956726a4fe55b16b1dbbfc16a715e39d0a82","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dotnet/orleans/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T22:54:52.880Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T18:37:24Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dotnet/orleans/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:56:04.612Z","hash":"0e94c27809cab30ae833945d7573956726a4fe55b16b1dbbfc16a715e39d0a82","originalBytes":17183,"storedBytes":17183,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["orleans","grain","grains","which","distributed","state","cluster","information","microsoft","other","streams","such","runtime","any","builds","data","model","net","persistence","see","silos","cloud","device","public","silo","systems","task","these","they","when","allows","available","developers","each","example","memory","new","placement","process","scalability","services","stable","status","timers","transactions","used","activated","amp","application","applications","automatically","azure","building","call","class","commands","core","csharp","enable","features","identity","interface","interfaces","need","one","project","reminders","server","single","stateless","stored","thermostat","using","without","above","addition","because","called","changes","clients","code","communicate","community","config","context","discord","documentation","enables","failures.","filters","following","framework","grains.","ithermostat","ithermostatcontrol","license","make","managed","multiple","nightly","onupdate","persistent","physical","point","profile","programming","provides",